#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0467 expect=violation domain=SUPPLB
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when --STDTC is present in a Findings general observation class dataset, where its use is not recommended.
#note "EC-36 SUPP pin: on a SUPP/SQ dataset the -- replacement is the EMPTY string (Python wildcard_replacement), so --STDTC resolves to the bare STDTC. The STDTC column below is deliberately contrived — no shipped rule pairs -- with a genuine SUPP column (QNAM/QVAL/IDVAR/...), so this is the only way to pin the empty-prefix semantics against a real rule. Before EC-36 the engine looked for SUPPLBSTDTC and never fired. ⚠ CLASS-UNREACHABLE IN PRODUCTION, recorded 2026-09-19 (review round 1): CDISC-CG0467 scopes Classes.Include [FINDINGS] - inherited from CORE-000207, which this fixture was MIGRATED from by PLAN-retire-core-family phase 5 - and SUPPLB is in no DomainClassMap family (only SUPPQUAL is) and the fixture carries RDOMAIN rather than DOMAIN, so CustomDomainClassDetector checks the BARE suffixes and QNAM makes it RELATIONSHIP, not FINDINGS. So DatasetRuleResolver does not emit the rule for this dataset and the scenario cannot fail for the reason it was written. The harness cannot say so: with no class= declaration AbstractRuleTestSuitesFactory.describeScopeMismatch routes the class axis to describeAdamClassMismatch, which deliberately refuses SDTM class scopes and returns null. ⛔ Do NOT delete it - it is now this rule's only SUPPLB coverage and ScenarioFixtureCoverageRatchetTest credits it; the production-reachable pair is the two class=FINDINGS LB fixtures beside it. ⚑ Measured against the OFFLINE class path (DomainClassMap then CustomDomainClassDetector), which is what an unlicensed run and this harness both use; with the CDISC Library reachable the product reverse-walk runs first and may answer differently for a SUPP or AP dataset - it cannot for AE, which is EVENTS on every path."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset SUPPLB label="Supplemental Qualifiers for LB"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QVAL type=Char label="Data Value"
col STDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time (contrived — see note)"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | LBSEQ | 1 | LBREASND | Not done | 2014-01-03
---
